# CI Gates

## Post-Push Poll (required)

After push to `main` or before release sign-off:

```bash
python3 scripts/agent-run.py check-github-ci --wait 300
```

## Gate Order (local)

1. `python3 scripts/agent-run.py update-deps` (dry-run; `--apply` only from `/update-deps` / `/ship`)
2. `scripts/watch-agent-gates.sh --once --autofix --scope auto` (after each AGENT feature step; `/gates` stays full)
3. `scripts/smoke-sprint.sh --require` after the sprint is all ✅ (every checked row; startup + load order). `/gates` uses `--if-complete`.
4. `scripts/feature-gate.sh --json` (RAM-capped parallel stacks on `multi`; `FEATURE_GATE_JOBS` override)
5. `pre-commit run --all-files` (optional if hooks installed)
6. `/prerelease` uses `pre-release-gate.sh --local` (no GitHub wait)
7. Push → `scripts/check-github-ci.sh --wait 300` (`/push`, `/regress` full gate)

**Autonomous rule:** On gate failure, agent auto-fixes from JSON output within feature scope; re-run until pass or 3-strike. Push still requires human approval.

## Do Not Mark Complete

- BUILD_PLAN `[AUTO]` items while CI / Security Scan / CodeQL red
- Sprint sign-off without `scripts/pre-release-gate.sh` on template releases
